# prompt as a guard. The round under review (36965b4) broke 19 high: 12 right replies refused (a load's line naming
# its transistor, and a second load of the asked kind meant to run on its own given to it as well), one drawn wrong (a
# switch twice), a needed pin called spare, a sensor's pin told to take a push button. The reading is now its surest
# form: one transistor, its line naming its pin (or none) and one tag no line has; no load in the block (the tag's
